{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_worker_mesh", "label": "Worker mesh", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "JavaScript is single-threaded per actor system, so parallelism inside one OS process needs several ActorSystems; the mesh runs one per worker thread and joins them into one cluster over MessageChannel \u2014 no TCP, no byte serialisation. For multi-process parallelism the regular cluster + TCP transport is the right tool."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workercluster", "label": "WorkerCluster", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Automates the broker/channel/handshake wiring the manual path spells out; the worker primitive is picked per runtime (Web Workers on Bun/Deno, node:worker_threads on Node) so the same code runs everywhere. spawn() leaves no live workers behind on failure because the instance owning them is never returned."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workerclusteroptions", "label": "WorkerClusterOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workernode_join", "label": "WorkerNode.join()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Must be called from inside an async main(): on Bun a top-level await in a worker suspends the module loader, so incoming messages never dispatch and the handshake hangs forever."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workerbroker", "label": "WorkerBroker", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One hub holding one MessagePort per node keeps wiring linear \u2014 N workers need N channels, not binomial(N,2) \u2014 at the cost of making the main thread the relay for all cross-node traffic."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_messagechanneltransport", "label": "MessageChannelTransport", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each node holds a single port, its own end of one channel to the broker, never an array."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_star_topology", "label": "Star, not a full mesh", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_failure_containment", "label": "Failure containment", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The framework subscribes the worker error event on every runtime; without that subscription Node re-raises the worker error on the host and Deno rejects an internal promise, and both exit 1 before restartPolicy is ever consulted. A failed respawn degrades the mesh by one worker rather than killing the host."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_restart_budget", "label": "Respawn backoff and restart budget", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each slot waits restartMinBackoffMs doubling to restartMaxBackoffMs with jitter and gets maxRestarts inside restartWindowMs; a replacement that never becomes ready counts against the same budget, so a permanently broken bootstrap stops instead of looping."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_structured_clone", "label": "Structured clone over postMessage", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Faster than framing and re-parsing text, and it carries the same rich types (Map, Set, Date) the TCP wire tagged JSON tree carries without the text round-trip."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_deno_worker_asymmetry", "label": "Deno confirms neither exit nor shutdown", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deno's parent-side Worker emits no close event, so restarts there are driven entirely by error and a worker that exits without throwing goes unnoticed; terminate() falls back to a short internal bound instead of a confirmation."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workerbackend", "label": "WorkerBackend", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_frame_validation", "label": "Broker frame address validation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The broker validates a frame's to and from addresses before routing, so one bad postMessage from a worker no longer throws inside the host's message listener; the payload is validated by the receiving transport, not by the broker."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_sharding_across_cores", "label": "Sharding across cores", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_worker_mesh", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workercluster", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workercluster", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workerclusteroptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workercluster", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workernode_join", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workercluster", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workerbroker", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workercluster", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workerbackend", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workercluster", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_restart_budget", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workerbroker", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_star_topology", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_star_topology", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_messagechanneltransport", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_worker_mesh", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_messagechanneltransport", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_messagechanneltransport", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_structured_clone", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_worker_mesh", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_failure_containment", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_failure_containment", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_restart_budget", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_failure_containment", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_deno_worker_asymmetry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_workerbroker", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_frame_validation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_worker_mesh", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_sharding_across_cores", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_sharding_across_cores", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_cluster_sharding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/worker-mesh.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_worker_mesh_worker_mesh", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_overview_cluster_sharding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confid